#---
# purpose: a function passed by name as a higher-order argument retains both a typed specialization and a callable entry, and its callable identity propagates through the call into the receiving parameter and its indirect call site.
#---
def double(x), do: x * 2
def apply2(f, x), do: f.(x)
def main() do
  dbg(apply2(double, 21))
end
